# Workspace exposure plugin contract (M5)

```yaml
doc_id: WORKSPACE-EXPOSURE-PLUGIN-CONTRACT
version: "2026-06-29-v1"
authority: docs/architecture/field-exposure-system.md
related:
  - docs/architecture/field-policy-system.md
  - docs/dev/workspace-integration-plugin-system.mdoc
implementation:
  sdk: packages/workspace-sdk/src/exposure/workspace-exposure-surface.ts
  denali: packages/workspaces/denali/src/exposure/denali-exposure.surface.ts
  starter: packages/workspaces/starter/src/exposure/starter-exposure.surface.ts
  api: apps/api/src/exposure/workspace-exposure-surfaces.service.ts
```

## Purpose

Field exposure answers **which registry fields may appear on a publication surface** for a given
audience and trigger. Integrations own **transport only**; workspace plugins declare **surface
defaults** consumed by the exposure control plane.

This contract mirrors `WorkspacePlugin.integrationSurface` — data-only manifest on the plugin,
validated at workspace package load time.

## Boundaries

| Layer | Owns |
| ----- | ---- |
| Field registry | Field identity, canonical paths, presentation metadata |
| Field policy (`fieldPolicy`) | Entity/workspace PDP states per `FieldPolicySurface` |
| **Exposure surface (`exposureSurface`)** | Surface id, audience, trigger labels, default visible field ids |
| API exposure engine | Intent persistence, resolver, dispatch selection |
| Integration plugin | Provider config, event policies, message templates |

Exposure surface ids (e.g. `public_list`, `telegram`) are **workspace-owned strings**. They must not
appear in SDK field-policy forbidden vocabulary lists — map to `FieldPolicySurface` in workspace
code (`map*ExposureSurfaceToFieldPolicySurface`).

## WorkspacePlugin.exposureSurface

Optional on `WorkspacePlugin`:

```typescript
readonly exposureSurface?: WorkspaceExposureSurface;
```

### Manifest shape

```typescript
type WorkspaceExposureSurface = {
  readonly manifestVersion: 1;
  readonly definitions: readonly WorkspaceExposureSurfaceDefinition[];
};

type WorkspaceExposureSurfaceDefinition = {
  readonly surface: string;
  readonly audience: string;
  readonly triggerLabel: string;       // operator-facing label
  readonly triggerStorageKey: string;  // persisted ExposureIntent.trigger
  readonly defaultFieldIds: readonly string[];
  readonly operatorSettingsVisible?: boolean; // default true; false hides from /settings/exposure surfaces panel
};
```

Validation: `validateExposureSurface()` — fail closed at workspace package module load (same pattern
as `validateIntegrationSurface()`).

### Denali reference

Five surfaces in `denali-exposure-surfaces.ts`; `telegram` has `operatorSettingsVisible: false`
(connection panel owns delivery field checklist). HTTP redaction bindings stay workspace-local
(`denali-catalog-exposure-bindings.ts`).

### Starter minimal slice

One surface: `public_list` / audience `public` / trigger `always` with field ids aligned to
`STARTER_FIELD_POLICY_MANIFEST` public/delivery rules.

## API resolution

`getWorkspaceExposureSurfaces` / `patchWorkspaceSurfaceExposureIntent` resolve
`resolveWorkspacePluginForType(workspaceType).exposureSurface` — **not** hardcoded Denali imports.

When `exposureSurface` is absent, settings surfaces API returns an empty list (patch → 403).

## Linkage to fieldPolicy

Workspace exposure definitions supply **default field id sets** for profile seeding. Field policy
manifest rules (`public_website`, `delivery`, `profile`) remain separate but should reference the
same field ids (Denali: `denali-field-policy.manifest.ts` imports from `denali-exposure-surfaces.ts`).

